  "body": "## The problem (discovered through live testing)\n\n`uv tool install` fails (exit 2) when a launcher is open, because a running launcher holds its own `.exe` shim **without `FILE_SHARE_DELETE`** — it can't be overwritten (os error 32). This is the hard Windows limit: \"running in memory\" doesn't bypass it; the lock is on the open handle's share mode.\n\nv5.3.3 tried renaming all shims aside, but that was too destructive — a failed install left canonical shims missing. **The user chose the hybrid approach.**\n\n## The fix\n\n1. Rename the tool dir aside, run `uv tool install`.\n2. The tool env + all **non-running** shims update; only the running launcher's shim errors (expected).\n3. Detect that expected failure **robustly**: check the fresh install actually landed in the tool dir (`uv-receipt.toml` names `$Version`). If so — keep the new install, report success, and launch the detached helper to finish the locked shim after the window closes.\n4. Any **other** uv failure restores the previous install (never leaves the user with no working tool).\n5. **No shims are renamed before install**, so a failure can never leave canonical shims missing.\n\nNet result: new `mcc-claude`/`mcc-server` sessions get the new version immediately; the one open window keeps old code until it closes, then the helper finishes its shim. No waiting for anything else.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New test: locked-shim case keeps the install and flags `NeedDeferredFinish`. All 6 rename tests pass; ruff/ty clean.\n- Live (5.3.3): verified the tool dir becomes the new version even when uv exits 2 on the locked shim.\n- **Live test pending post-merge** via the published URL.\n\nVersion 5.3.3 → 5.3.4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
