    "message": "fix(install): hybrid Windows update -- install now, finish only the running shim later\n\nThe rename-then-reinstall updated the tool dir and free shims immediately, but\nuv still fails copying a running launcher's own shim (os error 32, held without\nFILE_SHARE_DELETE). That failure is EXPECTED and harmless: the shim is\nversion-agnostic (its __main__.py shebangs to the tool-dir python path), so a\nnew launch of it already resolves the fresh tool dir. v5.3.3's \"rename all\nshims aside\" was too destructive -- a failed install left canonical shims\nmissing. Replaced it with the hybrid the user chose:\n\n- Rename the tool dir aside, run `uv tool install`. The tool env + all\n  non-running shims update; only the running launcher's shim errors.\n- Detect that expected failure robustly by checking the fresh install actually\n  landed in the tool dir (uv-receipt.toml names $Version). If so: keep the new\n  install, report success, and launch the detached helper to finish the locked\n  shim after the window closes. Any other uv failure restores the previous\n  install and is fatal.\n- No shims are renamed before install, so a failure can never leave canonical\n  shims missing.\n\nVerified live (5.3.3) that the tool dir becomes the new version even when uv\nexits 2 on the locked shim. New test: locked-shim case keeps the install and\nflags NeedDeferredFinish. All 6 rename tests pass; ruff/ty clean.\n\nVersion 5.3.3 -> 5.3.4.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
